      "localized": {
        "en-US": {
          "description": "<p>The phone app for <b>SuperAwesomeMagicalHealth</b>, a health server you run yourself. Your data stays on your server, and the private parts are encrypted there.</p>\n<p><b>Scores like Oura's.</b> Readiness, sleep and activity against your own baseline, with plain-English insights, stress and resilience, and trends over weeks and months.</p>\n<p><b>Your wearables, on your server.</b> Colmi rings over Bluetooth, Pebble and Garmin through Gadgetbridge, anything in Health Connect, and blood pressure monitors and glucose meters. The app carries their readings to your server.</p>\n<p><b>Log what matters to you.</b> Food (with barcode scanning), water, coffee and alcohol, weight, workouts, and how you feel. Turn on what else you want to keep track of:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Mood, a private journal, check-ins (PHQ-9, GAD-7) and calming tools, with support lines one tap away</li>\n<li>Your cycle, with predictions, and pregnancy, after a birth, perimenopause and menopause</li>\n<li>A bladder and bowel diary with pelvic floor exercises</li>\n<li>Medications with reminders, injection-site rotation and lab results</li>\n<li>Blood pressure and glucose, symptoms and migraines, habits, hormone therapy and appointments</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Reminders that work offline</b>, a weekly digest, reports for your doctor, and read-only sharing with someone who cares for you.</p>\n<p>You need a SuperAwesomeMagicalHealth server to sign in to: it runs in Podman or Docker (see the source code's README).</p>\n",
          "icon": "icon_9sXDTVQICS9NiyEF7AecLA9lURdJki5iat6dTMjaJxE=.png",
          "name": "SuperAwesomeMagicalHealth",
          "phoneScreenshots": [
            "1.png",
            "2.png",
            "3.png",
            "4.png",
            "5.png",
            "6.png",
            "7.png",
            "8.png"
          ],
          "summary": "Your own health server's app: scores, wearables, food, mood, cycle and more",
          "whatsNew": "SuperAwesomeMagicalHealth 0.6.2: safer, steadier, and reminders you can count on\n\nA careful review of the server, the web app and the phone app, and fixes for what it found.\n\nYour reminders\n- The phone app kept clearing reminders. If it couldn't reach your server when it started\n  (out of the house, on a plane, the server restarting), it cleared medication, habit, appointment\n  and bladder reminders. Routine reminders were cleared on every cold start. Now they stay put.\n- On\u2026 (more in the releas"
        }
      }
    }
